<interrogationes unitas="vicus_applicatio">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I start the vicus host app in a window or a terminal?
    <responsum symbolum="vicus_volumen_aperire vicus_applicatio_aedificare vicus_figurae vicus_imago_fons thema_initiare volumen_claudere" via="apps/vicus/vicus.c apps/vicus/vicus_terminalis.c">Call
      thema_initiare, open the volume with vicus_volumen_aperire
      (-fumus = temporary volume, -volumen PATH, default vicus.volumen),
      then vicus_applicatio_aedificare(&amp;app, piscina, intern, vol,
      latitudo, altitudo) with the size in our pixels. Hand the glue
      app.d, vicus_figurae(app.vicus) and vicus_imago_fons with ctx
      app.vicus; these never change afterwards. Close the volume with
      volumen_claudere at exit.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what does a fresh vicus open with, and which pane kinds can it show?
    <responsum symbolum="vicus_applicatio_aedificare vicus_genus_addere vicus_aperire">Ten
      tabs: 1 is scriba beside terminale, 2 scriba beside pictor, 3-10
      scriba beside scriba, plus the volantes (toast) layer on top. The
      registered kinds are scriba, pictor, terminale, calendarium,
      nomenclator, admonitiones, colloquia and volantes (the header's
      opening comment still lists only the first three). A tab whose
      kind is unknown or whose mount fails is skipped with its reason
      on stderr; the rest still run.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I open another pane or app from a scriba page in vicus?
    <responsum symbolum="vicus_applicatio_aedificare vicus_acervo_aperire iussum_registrare">Type
      a command on the page: $terminale, $scriba(name), $pictor(name),
      $calendarium, $agenda, $contacts, $notifications or $sessions
      opens that kind in the active tab's stack on the next pulse;
      $pictor-next, $pictor-prev and $pictor-new cycle or create
      pictures. A scriba page name may only use a-z, 0-9, _ and -.
      $dies or $dies(N) inserts the date N days from today as
      MM/DD/YYYY.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I make $question work, and why does it say there is no API port?
    <responsum symbolum="vicus_applicatio_quaestionis_portam_ponere VicusPortaQuaestionis" via="apps/vicus/vicus.c">The
      window app must give a port with
      vicus_applicatio_quaestionis_portam_ponere(&amp;app, &amp;porta):
      a VicusPortaQuaestionis with incipere, pulsare and abrumpere. The
      struct is copied. A NIHIL port, or one missing any of the three
      functions, clears it, and $question then reports "no API port
      (window app only)", which is what the terminal twin and the tests
      see.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why does vicus_applicatio not call the model API or parse Markdown itself?
    <responsum symbolum="VicusPortaQuaestionis quaestio_textum_planare" via="lib/vicus_applicatio.worklog.md include/vicus_quaestio.h">Plan
      ruling R9: the PORT plans the answer into logical lines
      (quaestio_textum_planare). If this file did it, it would include
      quaestio, vates and http/TLS, and the terminal twin and
      ludus_tessera's hand-made link list would drag in the whole API
      stack. The port types live in vicus_quaestio.h so the port can
      be built without including the whole app.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what happens on the page while $question streams an answer?
    <responsum symbolum="vicus_quaestio_disponere" via="lib/vicus_applicatio.worklog.md">The
      command is $question&lt;&gt;...&lt;/&gt; with free lines below it
      (otherwise "no free lines below"). The first call only defers
      ("asking ..."); the second starts the port and returns a job that
      each pulse lays out with vicus_quaestio_disponere into the FREE
      lines below the command, never beyond, and the command's head
      becomes &lt;answered&gt;. When the page is full the port is
      aborted and the text is cut at the last sentence or line end that
      fits (else at a word, with "..."); Esc adds [cancelled]; an error
      after some text adds [error: ...]; an error or an empty answer
      before any text leaves the page untouched. Caution (audit
      2026-10-18, unfixed): the per-pulse layout is not always bounded -
      an answer line whose indentation plus list/quote marker reaches
      the pane's inner width makes vicus_quaestio_disponere loop
      forever, and a hanging-indent answer can lay out to about 4x its
      length and overflow the responsum_aptare buffer (heap
      write past the piscina allocation).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I pass any text to vicus_quaestio_disponere?
    <responsum symbolum="vicus_quaestio_disponere quaestio_textum_planare">Planned
      text only (what quaestio_textum_planare gives): logical lines, a
      leading tab marks verbatim code that is hard-broken but never
      reflowed, and a list or quote marker after the indentation gets a
      hanging indent. It returns a newline, then &lt;answer&gt; ...
      &lt;/&gt; wrapped to width w with two columns of margin on each
      side (none below 24 columns), cut to fit l lines. Keep each
      line's indentation plus marker narrower than the inner width (w
      minus the margins): at or above it the wrapper stops advancing
      and the call never returns. Very deep indentation can also lay
      out longer than the buffer responsum_aptare allocates (input
      length x 2 + w x 4 + 64 bytes). Caution (audit 2026-10-18,
      unfixed): deep indentation is not needed - an ordinary hanging
      indent (a list or quote marker) can lay out to about 4x the input,
      and the second disponere pass in responsum_aptare then writes past
      its piscina allocation (heap overflow).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I let pictor panes paste images from the clipboard?
    <responsum symbolum="vicus_applicatio_imaginis_portam_ponere" via="apps/vicus/vicus.c">Call
      vicus_applicatio_imaginis_portam_ponere(&amp;app, porta, ctx) with
      a function returning an ImagoFructus. All pictor panes share one
      context and read the port at the moment of the paste, so panes
      mounted before the call see it too. NIHIL means no image source
      (the terminal twin has no Cocoa).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I turn on notifications, the sessions pane and tmux tracking?
    <responsum symbolum="vicus_applicatio_admonitiones_aperire">Call
      vicus_applicatio_admonitiones_aperire(&amp;app, via) once with the
      path of the praeconium log. Until then $notifications and
      $sessions are empty, nothing is read and tmux is never asked.
      Afterwards each pulse follows the log, and every 5 seconds
      terminal panes attached to tmux sessions are recorded (so a
      restore re-attaches) and detached ones forgotten. FALSUM if it is
      already open or the log cannot be followed.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
